l errors, placeholder text, and formatting inconsistencies. These are artifacts from the anonymized paper generation process and will be fully corrected in the final version. We will ensure all notation is consistent, figures/tables are correctly referenced, and the text is polished for clarity and professionalism.\n\n**4. Significance and Performance:** While constrained to patterns within 2-5 node graphlets (a limitation we explicitly discuss in Sec. G), our method shows significant and consistent performance gains in metrics like sub-recall and fidelity (Tables 1, 3, 4) over a wide range of baselines. More importantly, it provides explanations that are inherently connected, correspond to known structural units, and can be directly mapped to domain knowledge (as shown in the Gene dataset case study). We will strengthen the discussion of these quantitative and qualitative advantages in the revision.\n\nWe believe addressing these points, particularly the clarification of the decomposition's rationale and fixing presentation issues, will significantly improve the paper's soundness and impact."
