          "location": "Sections 4.1 and 4.2, Tables 3, 4, and the Abstract.",
          "explanation": "The submission explicitly documents and discusses this crucial limitation. The abstract states 'our layer underperforms state-of-the-art meta-learners in high-data regimes...' Table 3 shows MixER-10 underperforming the naive MoE (†) and single meta-learner on ODEBench-10B. Table 4 systematically compares MixER variants with baseline implementations (NCF*, CoDA*) on LV, GO, and SM problems, showing higher MSEs. The text in Sections 4.1 and 4.2 analyzes these results, attributing the underperformance to the partitioning of closely related data among experts, which limits each expert's exposure."
